SUMMARY:SMC Trail Work Volunteer Day
DESCRIPTION:South Mountain Conservancy Activities Meetup Group\n**TRAIL WO
 RK (which was canceled Sept. 13th due to steady rain) will continue rerout
 ing the Hogenauer Trail** (we are making progress!) up the slope and away 
 from recently installed property fences. **Meet At:** Dog Park/ Wildflower
  Preserve\, 11 Bear Lane\, Maplewood. From there\, we will walk to Crater 
 View on Crest drive and then to the Hogenauer trail work site. (Note: Whil
 e we normally meet the first Sudnay of each month\, this volunteer day was
  shifted after the Labor Day weekend.)\n\nTrail work is physically challen
 ging but very satisfying as we use hand tools to build and repair trails. 
 Participants must be 15+ years. Those younger than 18 must be accompanied 
 by an adult. Participants **should wear long pants** due to [ticks](https:
 //www.somocon.org/?page_id=193928&fb) and thron bushes and sturdy shoes\, 
 and bring gloves (though backup gloves will be available). Tools\, water\,
  and a snack will be provided. (Registration is not required though if you
  sign up on Meetup\, it helps us know how many tools to bring.) Only heavy
 \, steady rain cancels.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/somocon/events/316538128/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260913T120147Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260913T120147Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
