SUMMARY:Wildflower Sculpture Park Artist Walk & Talk
DESCRIPTION:South Mountain Conservancy Activities Meetup Group\n**Join the
  Root System artists for an artist walk and talk through the exhibition in
  the Wildflower Sculpture Park.**\n\nThe [Wildflower Sculpture Park](https
 ://www.somocon.org/visit/wildflower-sculpture-park/?mc_cid=887616f7ab&mc_e
 id=UNIQID) invites you to the opening of this year’s project\, **Root Sy
 stem**\, a collaborative\, site-responsive exploration of roots\, rhizomes
 \, and interconnected systems of life.\n\nCuratorial and artist talk will 
 begin at 3:30pm.\n\nArtists were encouraged to consider how ecological net
 works within the South Mountain Reservation connect to community\, history
 \, and ancestry\, and to propose work that engages themes of resilience\, 
 symbiosis\, and environmental stewardship.\n\nPresenting artists:\nANONDA 
 BELL\nCORRINE CARR\nCHRISTINE DACRUZ\nKATE EGGLESTON\nSAMAR HUSSAINI\nHAME
 WS\nKAREN LEO\nALESSANDRA PUGLISI\nJIMENA VEGA\nWILLA VUCETAJ\n\nQuestions
 ? [wildflowersculpture@somocon.org](mailto:wildflowersculpture@somocon.org
 )
